es at which the operator-based path is still viable for the release).\n- Confirm with the RHAISTRAT-7164 owners the expected delivery timing and the capabilities the modularized operator layer will expose for hosting PostgreSQL lifecycle management.\n- Select the provisioning path for the release: (A) operator-based self-provisioning, (B) gen-ai BFF-managed self-provisioning, or the degenerate fallback of bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n- Record the decision (decision record on the strategy ticket) naming the selected path, the owner of the PostgreSQL connection secret, and the per-namespace scoping confirmation for Gen AI Studio playgrounds.\n- Confirm per-namespace scoping for the playground (the strategy's open question; per-namespace is preferred and the per-instance consumer, Auto Rag, is decoupled to RHAISTRAT-7824).\n\nACs:\n- A decision record exists that selects exactly one provisioning path and states the go/no-go criteria and the evidence used (RHAISTRAT-7164 milestone dates confirmed with its owners).\n- The decision specifies who creates and manages the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace for the selected path.\n- The decision confirms the scoping model for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (per-namespace expected).\n- The selected path maps to one of the conditional branch plans attached to this strategy; the decision record names it.\n\nHLR Traceability: enables AC-1..AC-5 (gates all implementation). Hmm — traceability section should list HLRs covered. For an investigation, list \"enables AC-1, AC-3, AC-4\" etc. I'll say: Enables AC-1, AC-2, AC-3, AC-4, AC-5 (path selection gates every implementation of the default vector store).\n\n**E002 — Implementation: Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances**\n\nDescription: Delivers the Gen AI Studio side of the default vector store: when a playground with RAG capabilities is configured, the gen-ai backend-for-frontend sets the OGX instance's vector I