  configured; application storage stays on its existing default. All\n   SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration / storage-consolidation work was removed\n   from scope.\n4. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization,\n   In Progress).** The operator-based self-provisioning path requires the\n   RHOAI-controlled operator layer it delivers. The Staff Engineer requires a\n   go/no-go gate — modeled as Investigation E001 with conditional branches.\n5. **BFF-managed provisioning is the alternative fallback** if RHAISTRAT-7164\n   does not land in time (modeled as branch B), with bring-your-own\n   PostgreSQL as the recorded degenerate fallback.\n6. **Decouple from Auto Rag.** Auto Rag removed from affected components and\n   acceptance criteria; validation is scoped to Gen AI Studio playground RAG\n   only.\n7. **Performance/index/sizing open questions resolved as dev-experimentation\n   scope.** No strict latency SLAs; order-of-magnitude benchmark vs the\n   inline Milvus baseline; flat scan (no index) is sufficient. These became\n   acceptance criteria on the validation epic, not Investigation epics.\n8. **Existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable.** The\n   work concentration is infrastructure/provisioning, not vector_io provider\n   integration — no large OGX-distribution integration epic was generated.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Go/no-go gate: RHAISTRAT-7164 operator-layer availability and PostgreSQL provisioning path selection | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Validate pgvector as the default vector store for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A: RHAISTRAT-7164 lands) | Implementation (branch A) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path B: RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land) | Implementation (branch B) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n\n`epic_count` counts all epics including branches (5). Main-plan epics: E001,\nE002, E003.\n\n## Component Classification and Canonical Mapping\n\n- **Gen AI Studio (odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF, playground)** — active. Canonical\n  component `Gen AI Studio` used for the BFF wiring (E002), the BFF-managed\n  provisioning branch (BRANCH-B-E004), the operator-layer provisioning branch\n  (BRANCH-A-E004), the validation epic (E003), and the investigation (E001).\n  Note the span: BRANCH-A-E004 works in the dashboard operator layer delivered\n  by RHAISTRAT-7164; E003 spans the OGX distribution's pgvector provider.\n  `Gen AI Studio` is the single most-relevant canonical name for all of these;\n  no non-obvious mapping to other canonical names was needed.\n- **OGX distribution (ogx-distribution)** — **passive** (no code changes).\n  The remote pgvector vector_io provider already exists in the distribution\n  (corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ogx-distribution.md`:\n  vector I/O through Milvus, PGVector, or Qdrant backends). Validation of the\n  provider under playground RAG workloads is folded into E003's acceptance\n  criteria (same team validates — no separate validation epic). If validation\n  uncovers provider gaps, an `OGX Core` implementation epic must be added (see\n  Health Warnings).\n- **PostgreSQL with pgvector** — no new component onboarding: the existing\n  Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image ships pgvector (Staff Engineer\n  Correction 2), already used by model-registry-operator, with the\n  related-image env var already in the rhods-operator CSV. No repo-onboarding,\n  license-validation, or konflux-onboarding e