{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d556a28d-11db-42a7-8ac5-c08a77295a18","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b40ef5366d1d0658","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-ww59_x00/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A: RHAISTRAT-7164 lands)\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch plan, executed if the go/no-go decision confirms that the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the release: implement PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern, so every Gen AI Studio playground that needs RAG gets a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector provisioned automatically in its namespace — no manual user setup. The gen-ai BFF consumes the operator-managed connection when configuring the OGX instance's vector_io provider.\n\n## Scope\n\n- In the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard modularization, implement reconciliation of Gen AI Studio PostgreSQL instances: Deployment, Service, PVC, and connection Secret, using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image, which includes pgvector out of the box (no custom image build, no additional pipeline onboarding).\n- Follow the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern for the managed resource set and lifecycle behavior.\n- Define secret ownership: the operator creates and manages the PostgreSQL credentials consumed when the playground's OGX instance is configured.\n- Scope provisioning per playground namespace: one PostgreSQL instance per namespace.\n- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n- Preserve disconnected-install support by handling the PostgreSQL image reference through the existing related-image environment variable pattern already used for the model-registry PostgreSQL.\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DataScienceCluster becomes available (a later release), Gen AI Studio consumes the shared connection string rather than self-provisioning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- With the operator deployed, configuring a playground with RAG results in a PostgreSQL instance (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret) with pgvector available in the playground's namespace, with no manual user action.\n- An integration check demonstrates a playground RAG workflow functioning against an OGX instance whose vector_io provider uses the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL.\n- Automated tests cover the provisioning and cleanup lifecycle: creation, secret management, and deletion together with the owning playground.\n- The provisioned instance's resource requests/limits match the documented sizing starting point.\n- The operator's test suite passes and its build pipeline remains green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning): the provisioning this epic delivers.\n- AC-3 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment reconciled by the operator.\n- AC-4 (multi-tenant scoping): per-namespace provisioning.\n- AC-5 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments, bundled): resource requests/limits are set on the same Deployment this epic creates — same surface, not separately schedulable.\n- SC-2 (no additional manual setup steps): automatic provisioning removes manual setup.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81586,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8f6218420a36cf8","agent_id":"a5947f04ab1187a8b","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"fe8ced0b-4d73-4e7c-8bd5-9784cb023