{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b5830ff850c89af","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: 'Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A:\n4\t  RHAISTRAT-7164 lands)'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: Executed only if the go/no-go decision confirms RHAISTRAT-7164\n17\t    delivers the operator layer in time. If it does not land, this epic is removed\n18\t    and the BFF-managed provisioning branch (or the recorded bring-your-own-PostgreSQL\n19\t    fallback) is executed instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: -1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 0\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 1\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A: RHAISTRAT-7164 lands)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional branch plan, executed if the go/no-go decision confirms that the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the release: implement PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern, so every Gen AI Studio playground that needs RAG gets a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector provisioned automatically in its namespace — no manual user setup. The gen-ai BFF consumes the operator-managed connection when configuring the OGX instance's vector_io provider.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- In the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard modularization, implement reconciliation of Gen AI Studio PostgreSQL instances: Deployment, Service, PVC, and connection Secret, using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image, which includes pgvector out of the box (no custom image build, no additional pipeline onboarding).\n45\t- Follow the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern for the managed resource set and lifecycle behavior.\n46\t- Define secret ownership: the operator creates and manages the PostgreSQL credentials consumed when the playground's OGX instance is configured.\n47\t- Scope provisioning per playground namespace: one PostgreSQL instance per namespace.\n48\t- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing.\n49\t- Preserve disconnected-install support by handling the PostgreSQL image reference through the existing related-image environment variable pattern already used for the model-registry PostgreSQL.\n50\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DataScienceCluster becomes available (a later release), Gen AI Studio consumes the shared connection string rather than self-provisioning.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- With the operator deployed, configuring a playground with RAG results in a PostgreSQL instance (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret) with pgvector available in the playground's namespace, with no manual user action.\n55\t- An integration check demonstrates a playground RAG workflow functioning against an OGX instance whose vector_io provider uses the operator-provisioned PostgreSQL.\n56\t- Automated tests cover the provisioning and cleanup lifecycle: creation, secret management, and deletion together with the owning playground.\n57\t- The provisioned instance's resource requests/limits match the documented sizing starting point.\n58\t- The operator's test suite passes and its build pipeline remains green.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning): the provisioning this epic delivers.\n63\t- AC-3 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): PostgreSQL runs as its own deployment reconciled by the operator.\n64\t- AC-4 (multi-tenant scoping): per-namespace provisioning.\n65\t- AC-5 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments, bundled): resource requests/limits are set on the same Deployment this epic creates — same surface, not separately schedulable.\n66\t- SC-2 (no additional manual setup steps): automatic provisioning removes manual setup.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e3984cba26ba204","agent_id":"aaec9aa803340dfa3","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"199a33ef-3ef3-4a0b-add7-75cc119d3951","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:40:21.727Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b5830ff850c89af","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
