deferrable independent features.\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\nThe diagram (`graph TD`, dependency → dependent) matches frontmatter\n`dependencies` exactly in both directions: E001→E002, E001→BRANCH-A-E004,\nE001→BRANCH-B-E004, E002→E003. No cycles, no invalid edges. Both branch files\nset `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001`\n(the main-plan Investigation that selects them), and no main-plan epic lists a\nbranch epic in its dependencies. The coupling between E002/E003 and the\nselected provisioning branch is correctly expressed as acceptance criteria on\nboth sides rather than DAG edges — the rule-compliant shape for\nconditionally-existing nodes. Critical path is 3 (E001→E002→E003), appropriate\nfor an M-size strategy with no new component onboarding. No\nkonflux-onboarding, license-validation, or repo-onboarding epics exist, so\nRules 7/8/10 parallelism is not applicable. Cross-check of epic content found\nno uncaptured data/artifact dependency: the PostgreSQL connection E002\nconsumes is produced by exactly one selected branch, which cannot be a DAG\nedge by contract and is instead AC-gated on both sides.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\nAll epics share team Gen AI Studio, so no cross-team bundling. Component\n`Gen AI Studio` is canonical (validator-confirmed); the summary explicitly\nflags the span (BRANCH-A-E004 in the operator layer, E003 across the OGX\ndistribution's provider) and the ogx-distribution is correctly classified\npassive with a concrete observable re-split trigger (validation uncovers\nprovider gaps → add an `OGX Core` epic) recorded in Health Warnings. No epic\nexceeds ~2 weeks: E002 is a configuration-wiring sweep over one BFF code path;\neach branch epic is one provisioning implementation following a named\nprecedent pattern; E003 is one validation/benchmark effort. No scope\nduplication: E002 (vector_io wiring) and the branch epics (PostgreSQL\ninfrastructure) are complementary halves of AC-1, not competing