is accounted for: the six acceptance criteria appear as\n129\tAC-1..AC-5 plus the documented Auto Rag removal; the three success criteria\n130\tare mapped (SC-3 as whole-plan outcome, justified); both strategy open\n131\tquestions are explicitly dispositioned (scoping model resolved by E001/E002\n132\tscope; migration path as E002's override AC); Correction 3's no-migration\n133\tconstraint is carried into E002's scope and testable AC. Staff Engineer\n134\tcontext is carried forward: resource sizing starting point (E003 + both\n135\tbranches), portability to the 3.6 shared platform database (both branches),\n136\tbenchmark-vs-baseline framing (E003), and the RHAISTRAT-7474 unblocking note\n137\t(Health Warnings). Conditional branches cover both bounded outcomes of the\n138\tgate (A: operator path; B: BFF-managed path), and the degenerate third\n139\toutcome (bring-your-own PostgreSQL) is explicitly recorded in E001's scope and\n140\tBRANCH-B's gate_failure_impact as a no-code documented fallback — nothing is\n141\tsilently dropped. One watch item, not a gap requiring revision: BRANCH-A\n142\tpreserves disconnected-install support via the related-image env var pattern,\n143\twhile BRANCH-B's scope does not explicitly state how the PostgreSQL image\n144\treference is resolved for disconnected installs — worth adding when that\n145\tbranch is executed (see issues list).\n146\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0254eeaf743f1aa","agent_id":"a920bdac4fdce0601","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"0eb2391a-dcb5-4734-9e80-478ba0d40e3d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:43:30.127Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9513768bf4b95998","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
