{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d507b50d46ad1fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004 (Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio and Auto Rag)\n10\t\n11\tStrategy status Release Pending, priority Blocker. The full strategy attachment\n12\t(`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) was not provisioned in this workspace, so the\n13\trequirement set is derived from the Jira description's Acceptance Criteria and\n14\tSuccess Criteria as corrected by the (extensive, non-empty) Staff Engineer\n15\tInput, which takes precedence over the AI-generated technical approach.\n16\tAuto Rag is removed from scope per Staff Engineer Input (decoupled to\n17\tRHAISTRAT-7824, targeting RHOAI 3.6).\n18\t\n19\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n20\t\n21\tEach override below changes the decomposition relative to what the\n22\tAI-generated strategy attachment would have implied:\n23\t\n24\t1. **OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL (Correction 1).** OGX defaults to\n25\t   SQLite for application storage; the BFF hardcodes SQLite for playground\n26\t   OGX instances. Introducing PostgreSQL for vector storage is new work, not\n27\t   an extension of existing infrastructure — hence the provisioning epics.\n28\t2. **A Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector already exists (Correction\n29\t   2).** The model-registry-operator already auto-provisions this image and\n30\t   the related-image env var is already in the rhods-operator CSV for\n31\t   disconnected installs. The strategy's 1-2 sprint image-onboarding estimate\n32\t   is eliminated: **no custom image build epic and no Konflux onboarding epic\n33\t   were generated.**\n34\t3. **Vector storage and application storage are independent configurations\n35\t   (Correction 3).** Only the vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`) is\n36\t   configured; application storage stays on its existing default. All\n37\t   SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration / storage-consolidation work was removed\n38\t   from scope.\n39\t4. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization,\n40\t   In Progress).** The operator-based self-provisioning path requires the\n41\t   RHOAI-controlled operator layer it delivers. The Staff Engineer requires a\n42\t   go/no-go gate — modeled as Investigation E001 with conditional branches.\n43\t5. **BFF-managed provisioning is the alternative fallback** if RHAISTRAT-7164\n44\t   does not land in time (modeled as branch B), with bring-your-own\n45\t   PostgreSQL as the recorded degenerate fallback.\n46\t6. **Decouple from Auto Rag.** Auto Rag removed from affected components and\n47\t   acceptance criteria; validation is scoped to Gen AI Studio playground RAG\n48\t   only.\n49\t7. **Performance/index/sizing open questions resolved as dev-experimentation\n50\t   scope.** No strict latency SLAs; order-of-magnitude benchmark vs the\n51\t   inline Milvus baseline; flat scan (no index) is sufficient. These became\n52\t   acceptance criteria on the validation epic, not Investigation epics.\n53\t8. **Existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable.** The\n54\t   work concentration is infrastructure/provisioning, not vector_io provider\n55\t   integration — no large OGX-distribution integration epic was generated.\n56\t\n57\t## Epic List\n58\t\n59\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n60\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n61\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Go/no-go gate: RHAISTRAT-7164 operator-layer availability and PostgreSQL provisioning path selection | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n63\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Validate pgvector as the default vector store for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n64\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path A: RHAISTRAT-7164 lands) | Implementation (branch A) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n65\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E004 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (path B: RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land) | Implementation (branch B) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n66\t\n67\t`epic_count` counts all epics including branches (5). Main-plan epics: E001,\n68\tE002, E003.\n69\t\n70\t## Component Classification and Canonical Mapping\n71\t\n72\t- **Gen AI Studio (odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF, playground)** — active. Canonical\n73\t  component `Gen AI Studio` used for the BFF wiring (E002), the BFF-managed\n74\t  provisioning branch (BRANCH-B-E004), the operator-layer provisioning branch\n75\t  (BRANCH-A-E004), the validation epic (E003), and the investigation (E001).\n76\t  Note the span: BRANCH-A-E004 works in the dashboard operator layer delivered\n77\t  by RHAISTRAT-7164; E003 spans the OGX distribution's pgvector provider.\n78\t  `Gen AI Studio` is the single most-relevant canonical name for all of these;\n79\t  no non-obvious mapping to other canonical names was needed.\n80\t- **OGX distribution (ogx-distribution)** — **passive** (no code changes).\n81\t  The remote pgvector vector_io provider already exists in the distribution\n82\t  (corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ogx-distribution.md`:\n83\t  vector I/O through Milvus, PGVector, or Qdrant backends). Validation of the\n84\t  provider under playground RAG workloads is folded into E003's acceptance\n85\t  criteria (same team validates — no separate validation epic). If validation\n86\t  uncovers provider gaps, an `OGX Core` implementation epic must be added (see\n87\t  Health Warnings).\n88\t- **PostgreSQL with pgvector** — no new component onboarding: the existing\n89\t  Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image ships pgvector (Staff Engineer\n90\t  Correction 2), already used by model-registry-operator, with the\n91\t  related-image env var already in the rhods-operator CSV. No repo-onboarding,\n92\t  license-validation, or konflux-onboarding epic is generated.\n93\t- **Auto Rag** — removed from scope per Staff Engineer Input (RHAISTRAT-7824).\n94\t\n95\tTeams were inferred (Gen AI Studio / dashboard-crimson-scrum) because the\n96\tImpacted Teams table lives in the unavailable attachment — see Health\n97\tWarnings.\n98\t\n99\t## Dependency DAG\n100\t\n101\t```mermaid\n102\tgraph TD\n103\t    E001[\"E001 Go/no-go: provisioning path (Investigation)\"] --> E002[\"E002 BFF pgvector vector_io wiring\"]\n104\t    E001 --> BAE004[\"BRANCH-A-E004 Operator-based provisioning (path A)\"]\n105\t    E001 --> BBE004[\"BRANCH-B-E004 BFF-managed provisioning (path B)\"]\n106\t    E002 --> E003[\"E003 Validation & benchmark\"]\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\tBranch epics are conditional alternatives attached to E001's outcome; exactly\n110\tone of BRANCH-A-E004 / BRANCH-B-E004 executes. They are excluded from the\n111\tmain-plan critical path.\n112\t\n113\t## DAG Justification\n114\t\n115\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n116\t|------|------|-----------|\n117\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The selected provisioning path determines how the gen-ai BFF sources the PostgreSQL connection (operator-managed secret vs BFF-created). True gate: `rewrite` — the integration approach changes with the outcome. |\n118\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E004 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | The operator-based provisioning epic exists only if outcome A (RHAISTRAT-7164 lands in time). True gate: `remove`. |\n119\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E004 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | The BFF-managed provisioning epic exists only if outcome B (RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land). True gate: `remove`. |\n120\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12/14 (consumer builds against producer) | The validation epic exercises the wired pgvector vector_io configuration; it cannot start before the wiring implementation exists. |\n121\t\n122\tNotable non-edges:\n123\t\n124\t- **No edge between E002 and either branch epic.** E002 consumes \"the\n125\t  PostgreSQL connection available in the playground namespace\" whichever way\n126\t  it is provisioned; the branch epics own creating it. Their integration is\n127\t  expressed as acceptance criteria on both sides (each branch epic must\n128\t  result in a working playground-RAG-capable instance; E003 validates\n129\t  end-to-end), never as a DAG edge — a main-plan epic must not depend on a\n130\t  branch epic.\n131\t- **E003 → branch epic edge is impossible by contract** (branch epics are not\n132\t  main-plan nodes). E003's acceptance criteria require an environment with\n133\t  the default vector store provisioned via the selected path; sequencing\n134\t  against the selected branch plan is managed at execution time. Each branch\n135\t  epic carries its own \"playground with RAG works against the provisioned\n136\t  instance\" integration criterion so the coupling is testable on both sides.\n137\t- **No konflux-onboarding / repo-onboarding / license-validation epics** —\n138\t  Staff Engineer Correction 2 eliminates image onboarding entirely; all work\n139\t  lands in existing repos with existing pipelines.\n140\t\n141\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n142\t\n143\tRequirement IDs are the strategy's Acceptance Criteria (the HLR section is in\n144\tthe unavailable attachment), renumbered after removing the Auto Rag criterion\n145\tper Staff Engineer Input:\n146\t\n147\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n148\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n149\t| AC-1: Default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004 | Wiring (E002) plus exactly one provisioning branch. |\n150\t| AC-2: Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with no loss of capability | P0 | E002, E003 | Implementation + validation evidence. |\n151\t| AC-3: Default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004 | Remote pgvector provider + separately deployed PostgreSQL. |\n152\t| AC-4: Scoped for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation) | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004, E003 | Per-namespace scoping confirmed by E001; isolation verified in E003. |\n153\t| AC-5: Lightweight for resource-constrained environments | P1 | BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004 (bundled), E003 (bundled) | (bundled) in the branch epics: resource requests/limits are set on the same Deployment the epic creates — same surface, not separately schedulable. (bundled) in E003: the footprint measurement is produced by the same benchmark/validation run — a separate epic would duplicate the harness. |\n154\t| SC-1: No functional regression when inline providers are removed | P0 | E002, E003 | Delivered by the E002+E003 chain. |\n155\t| SC-2: No additional manual setup steps vs current experience | P0 | BRANCH-A-E004, BRANCH-B-E004 | The provisioning path removes manual setup; E002 makes it transparent to the user. |\n156\t| SC-3: RHAISTRAT-7474 unblocked | P0 | (whole plan) | Outcome of completing the main plan; not a separate epic. |\n157\t| Removed: Auto Rag functions with the default vector store | — | — | Removed per Staff Engineer Input; addressed in RHAISTRAT-7824 (RHOAI 3.6). |\n158\t\n159\tOpen questions from the strategy and their disposition:\n160\t\n161\t- **Scoping model (per-namespace vs per-instance):** resolved by Staff\n162\t  Engineer Input direction — per-namespace preferred, and the per-instance\n163\t  consumer (Auto Rag) is decoupled. Captured as scope/AC on E002 and both\n164\t  branch epics; E001 confirms it. Not an Investigation epic.\n165\t- **Migration path to a production-grade vector database:** does not change\n166\t  which epics exist — captured as an overridability acceptance criterion on\n167\t  E002 (the OGX vector