{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f69de840efc67eb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Go/no-go gate: RHAISTRAT-7164 operator-layer availability and PostgreSQL provisioning\n4\t  path selection'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Go/no-go gate: RHAISTRAT-7164 operator-layer availability and PostgreSQL provisioning path selection\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating decision: whether the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) will deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the target release, and therefore which provisioning path the default vector store takes — operator-based self-provisioning of PostgreSQL/pgvector in that operator layer, self-provisioning managed directly by the gen-ai backend-for-frontend, or (as a degenerate fallback) requiring users to bring their own PostgreSQL. The Staff Engineer Input identifies the operator layer as a hard dependency for the operator-based path and requires the development team to define a go/no-go gate as part of sprint planning. The answer determines which downstream implementation epics exist, so the decomposition carries a conditional branch plan per outcome.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Define the go/no-go gate criteria tied to RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery milestones — the dates and scope points at which the operator-based path is still viable for the release.\n35\t- Confirm with the RHAISTRAT-7164 owners the expected delivery timing and the capabilities the modularized operator layer will expose for hosting PostgreSQL lifecycle management.\n36\t- Select the provisioning path for the release: operator-based self-provisioning (path A), gen-ai BFF-managed self-provisioning (path B), or bring-your-own PostgreSQL as the recorded fallback if neither self-provisioning path is viable.\n37\t- Specify, for the selected path, who creates and manages the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace (operator, BFF, or user).\n38\t- Confirm the scoping model for Gen AI Studio playgrounds — per-namespace is the preferred model and the per-instance consumer (Auto Rag) is decoupled to RHAISTRAT-7824, so per-namespace is expected to be confirmed.\n39\t- Record the decision on the strategy ticket as a decision record naming the selected path and the branch plan to execute.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A decision record exists on the strategy ticket that selects exactly one provisioning path, states the go/no-go criteria, and cites the evidence used (RHAISTRAT-7164 milestone confirmation from its owners).\n44\t- The decision record specifies the owner of the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace for the selected path.\n45\t- The decision record confirms the scoping model for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (per-namespace expected).\n46\t- The decision maps to one of the conditional branch plans attached to the gating decision, and the record names the selected plan.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- Enables AC-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store), AC-3 (separate-process vector store), AC-4 (multi-tenant scoping), and SC-2 (no additional manual setup steps): the path selection determines which provisioning implementation delivers these.\n51\t- Enables AC-2 (playground RAG with no loss of capability) and SC-1 (no functional regression): all downstream capability work is gated on this decision.\n52\t- Resolves the strategy's scoping open question (per-namespace vs per-instance) and the go/no-go requirement raised in the Staff Engineer Input.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-971183a0754b174e","agent_id":"a0de9fd64ece51da2","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"9bcf44b8-6343-4d38-8bf5-c1567ec873f6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:44:41.052Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f69de840efc67eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
