{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82e37f1fa3051caa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\t  OGX instances\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the go/no-go decision selects a different provisioning path,\n16\t    how this epic's deliverable sources the PostgreSQL connection (operator-managed\n17\t    secret vs BFF-created) is reworked; the vector_io wiring itself is stable across\n18\t    paths.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Configure the remote pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the Gen AI Studio side of the default vector store: when a playground with RAG capabilities is configured, the gen-ai backend-for-frontend sets the OGX instance's vector I/O provider to the remote pgvector provider, pointed at the PostgreSQL connection available in the playground's namespace. This replaces reliance on the inline Milvus provider that RHAISTRAT-7474 removes from the OGX distribution, keeping playground RAG working out of the box. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable; the work is the configuration wiring in the gen-ai BFF code path where OGX instances are created and configured for playgrounds today.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- In the gen-ai BFF code path that creates and configures OGX instances for playgrounds, set the vector_io provider configuration to the remote pgvector provider (the distribution's supported pgvector provider activation), using the PostgreSQL connection available in the playground's namespace — regardless of whether that connection is provided by an operator or created by the BFF itself.\n45\t- Scope the configuration per playground namespace (one vector store per namespace), matching the confirmed scoping model.\n46\t- Leave the OGX application storage backend configuration untouched (it remains on its existing default): vector storage and application storage are independent configurations, and no storage migration is in scope.\n47\t- Keep the vector_io provider selection overridable so an external, production-grade vector database can be configured instead of the default — this is both the migration path raised in the strategy's open questions and the rollback path for the replaced inline-provider capability.\n48\t- Update playground documentation references that fall out of this change incidentally (no substantive new content authoring).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- An automated test demonstrates that configuring a playground with RAG results in an OGX instance whose vector_io provider is the remote pgvector provider using the PostgreSQL connection available in the playground's namespace.\n53\t- An automated test demonstrates per-namespace scoping: playgrounds in different namespaces use separate vector store instances.\n54\t- An automated test demonstrates that the OGX application storage backend configuration is unchanged by this work (vector storage configuration only).\n55\t- An automated test demonstrates that the vector_io provider can be overridden to an external vector database configuration (migration/rollback path).\n56\t- The gen-ai BFF test suite passes and the build pipeline remains green.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box): delivers the wiring that makes the provisioned PostgreSQL the playground's default vector store.\n61\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of capability): the wired provider is what the playground RAG workflows run against; capability evidence is completed by the validation epic.\n62\t- AC-3 (separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): the remote pgvector provider runs outside the OGX process, unlike the inline provider it replaces.\n63\t- AC-4 (multi-tenant scoping): per-namespace configuration of the vector store.\n64\t- SC-1 (no functional regression when inline providers are removed): the replacement configuration this epic delivers.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-971183a0754b174e","agent_id":"a0de9fd64ece51da2","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"dd6a1062-c75d-495d-85d8-0d01f42ef853","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:44:41.899Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82e37f1fa3051caa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
