{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0640a35e9b57991","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Validate pgvector as the default vector store for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\t  RAG workflows\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Validate pgvector as the default vector store for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the strategy's validation evidence that the pgvector-backed default vector store preserves Gen AI Studio playground RAG capability: end-to-end validation of playground RAG workflows against the default vector store provisioned via the selected provisioning path, a benchmark comparing pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline, per-namespace isolation verification, and a resource-footprint assessment with a sizing recommendation. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the default instance targets development experimentation: no strict latency SLAs are required — the benchmark verifies pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline, and flat scan (no index) is the expected access path for typical playground document sets. Auto Rag compatibility is explicitly out of scope (addressed by RHAISTRAT-7824).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Capture the inline Milvus baseline for representative playground RAG operations (document ingestion, embedding, retrieval) while the inline provider is still available.\n40\t- Benchmark the pgvector default vector store on the same operations and compare order of magnitude against the baseline.\n41\t- End-to-end validation of playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval-augmented generation) against the default vector store provisioned via the selected provisioning path, verifying no loss of current capability.\n42\t- Verify per-namespace isolation: vector data in one namespace is not visible to another.\n43\t- Record the observed resource footprint of the default vector store and a sizing recommendation starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits, confirming the default is lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments.\n44\t- Record any gaps found in the OGX distribution's remote pgvector provider under playground workloads (the distribution is otherwise expected to need no changes).\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A benchmark report exists comparing the inline Milvus baseline and pgvector results for representative playground RAG operations, showing pgvector within the same order of magnitude as the baseline.\n49\t- An end-to-end validation record exists showing playground RAG workflows functioning against the default vector store with no loss of current capability.\n50\t- An isolation validation record exists demonstrating that cross-namespace vector data access is not possible.\n51\t- A sizing recommendation records the observed resource footprint and the recommended requests/limits for the default vector store.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with no loss of capability): the end-to-end validation and benchmark evidence.\n56\t- AC-4 (multi-tenant scoping): the per-namespace isolation verification.\n57\t- AC-5 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments, bundled): the footprint measurement is produced by the same validation and benchmark run — a separate epic would duplicate the harness.\n58\t- SC-1 (no functional regression when inline providers are removed): the comparison against the inline Milvus baseline is the regression evidence.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-971183a0754b174e","agent_id":"a0de9fd64ece51da2","session_id":"0064224b-16f9-4322-85c9-ccae87fefaaf","uuid":"be137301-fa2a-49f2-b4f5-4e565c8800b4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:44:42.726Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0640a35e9b57991","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
